8e02c64f-f574-4bda-8d57-c22d9ed5dba8	392e146e-92d3-486c-a4f3-efa54a628127	d934bedc-bbe4-4d95-adbc-d6f3c6afd151	live_move_3_92bc8620	move	worked_example	\N	{"id": "live_move_3_92bc8620", "type": "worked_example", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx", "blockId": "live_block_3_060709b3", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx\\",\\"type\\":\\"worked_example\\",\\"problemStatement\\":\\"Compute the integral ∫ x e^x dx using integration by parts. Show choice of u and dv, find du and v, apply the formula, and simplify.\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"step-1\\",\\"title\\":\\"Choose u and dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Pick u = x (a polynomial whose derivative simplifies) and dv = e^x dx (easy to integrate). This pairing follows the heuristic 'choose u to simplify when differentiated.'\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Before proceeding, predict what du will be when u = x.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv: du = 1 dx, and ∫ e^x dx = e^x so v = e^x. These give the components needed for the formula.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Predict the next algebraic expression when applying the formula u·v − ∫ v·du.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply the integration-by-parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Apply ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du. Substitute u = x, v = e^x, du = dx to get x e^x − ∫ e^x dx.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No prediction required.)\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4\\",\\"title\\":\\"Finish and simplify\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Integrate the remaining term: ∫ e^x dx = e^x. So the result is x e^x − e^x + C. Factor if desired: e^x(x − 1) + C.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No prediction required.)\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Explain in one sentence why choosing u = x and dv = e^x dx was appropriate for this integral.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Standard calculus integration-by-parts formula\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Any first-year calculus textbook or course notes covering ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du.\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 61623, "completedAtMs": 61623, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Resolved topic profile recommends a worked example next in the practicePattern.", "Student completed prerequisite check and goal framing; they committed to attempting one short example (cheap commitment).", "Only one move remains and the topic's mathematical load is high — a single focused worked example (with one prediction point) is time-efficient.", "Worked examples provide concrete procedural scaffolding needed for integration by parts."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student attempts and completes one worked example (∫ x e^x dx) showing the choice of u and dv, performing u-substitution for du, integrating dv, applying the formula, and simplifying; plus a short justification for why the chosen u/dv pairing was appropriate. The student also makes (or answers) one brief prediction about the next algebraic step before it's revealed.", "firstContentAtMs": 61623, "studentSafeReason": "A worked example is the highest-value next step: the student has passed prerequisites and agreed to attempt a short example, and we have one remaining move so a focused procedural worked example will build procedural fluency safely.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
