785665dd-2523-4ca7-8971-cfbe5b103e67	392e146e-92d3-486c-a4f3-efa54a628127	12de5d21-7d4d-419f-a678-4010a3438f4c	live_move_2_506d633c	move	goal_frame	\N	{"id": "live_move_2_506d633c", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "12-minute goal: apply integration by parts", "blockId": "live_block_2_dea2fca5", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"12-minute goal: apply integration by parts\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 12 minutes you will learn and practise using the integration-by-parts formula to compute an integral and explicitly justify your choice of u and dv.\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":12,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"State the integration-by-parts formula and why it follows from the product rule\\",\\"Choose u and dv for a given integrand and set up the resulting integrals\\",\\"Carry out the integration and briefly justify that your choice of u and dv made the integral simpler\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 25776, "completedAtMs": 25776, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Resolved topic profile's opening pattern: prerequisite_check then goal_frame.", "Session has limited remaining moves and ~15 minutes available; a concise goal frame helps prioritise next worked examples.", "Prerequisite check completed successfully so it's appropriate to commit to a short actionable learning outcome now."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student accepts the short timeboxed learning outcome (cheap commitment) and briefly indicates whether they'd prefer a procedural worked example or an exam-styled example, which will guide the next move.", "firstContentAtMs": 25776, "studentSafeReason": "After confirming the mandatory prerequisite (product rule), set a clear short goal so the student knows what they will be able to do next and we can timebox the interaction to fit the remaining session time.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
34de854c-374c-4682-9ff7-623446f3e427	392e146e-92d3-486c-a4f3-efa54a628127	12de5d21-7d4d-419f-a678-4010a3438f4c	live_move_3_b00db2e9	move	worked_example	\N	{"id": "live_move_3_b00db2e9", "type": "worked_example", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx", "blockId": "live_block_3_201a2f60", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx\\",\\"type\\":\\"worked_example\\",\\"problemStatement\\":\\"Compute the integral ∫ x e^x dx using integration by parts. Before the solution, state which part you choose as u and which as dv and why.\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"step-1-choose\\",\\"title\\":\\"Choose u and dv (your prediction)\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Pick u and dv so that du is simpler than u and dv is easy to integrate. For ∫ x e^x dx, a common choice is u = x (so du = dx) and dv = e^x dx (so v = e^x), because differentiating x simplifies it and integrating e^x is straightforward.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Before I show the solution, write which you choose: u = ? and dv = ? and one short reason for your choice.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2-differentiate-integrate\\",\\"title\\":\\"Compute du and v\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv. With u = x, du = dx. With dv = e^x dx, integrate to get v = e^x. These are the pieces needed for the formula ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3-apply-formula\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply integration-by-parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Use ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du. Substitute u = x, v = e^x, du = dx to get ∫ x e^x dx = x e^x − ∫ e^x dx. The remaining integral ∫ e^x dx equals e^x, so the expression becomes x e^x − e^x + C.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4-simplify-and-check\\",\\"title\\":\\"Simplify and verify by differentiating\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Factor e^x: x e^x − e^x = e^x(x − 1) + C. Differentiate e^x(x − 1): derivative = e^x(x − 1) + e^x(1) = x e^x, which matches the integrand, so the result is correct.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"State the final antiderivative you expect and one sentence checking it by differentiation.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Confirm you chose u and dv (and why), and write the final antiderivative. If your choice was different from u = x, dv = e^x dx, briefly explain how your alternate choice leads to a correct result or why it is less convenient.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Standard calculus reference\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Integration by parts formula: ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du (commonly shown in introductory calculus texts).\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 44691, "completedAtMs": 44691, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends a worked_example after goal framing and prerequisite checks.", "Session has one move remaining and ~14–15 minutes left — a single worked example fits the timebox.", "Worked examples are high-value for procedural, symbolic skills like integration by parts."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student computes the integral correctly (or with minor arithmetic errors) and explicitly states which part was chosen as u and which as dv and why.", "firstContentAtMs": 44691, "studentSafeReason": "A worked example will let the student practice applying the formula and justify choices of u and dv; with only one move left, a focused procedural example is the most efficient next step.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
