nted line, state the full sequence of printed lines for all iterations, in order.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Confirm you predicted the first printed line correctly and that the final sum_so_far is 10.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Example code\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Small illustrative Python snippet showing sequential iteration over a list.\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 48786, "completedAtMs": 48786, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends worked_example after a prediction to consolidate mechanics", "Remaining time and one move left — a short worked example is efficient", "Prior prediction revealed readiness to practice procedural execution", "Worked example supports sequential representation of iteration"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student correctly follows the worked example steps, predicts intermediate printed values at one prediction point, and completes one short practice trace without errors.", "firstContentAtMs": 48786, "studentSafeReason": "A worked example lets the student see loop mechanics (iteration order, variable updates, prints) with minimal cognitive load and gives a scaffolded task to practice safely.", "studentConsentRequired": false}	2026-08-09 18:35:00.905796+03
