luency with differentiation of products.", "We have time for a short readiness check (cheap commitment)."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student correctly answers two short questions: (1) state the product rule, and (2) differentiate a simple product (e.g., d/dx[x^2 sin x]).", "firstContentAtMs": 19009, "studentSafeReason": "Confirming the student can differentiate products is low-risk and needed before teaching integration by parts.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_144194c3", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Goal: integration by parts practice", "blockId": "live_block_2_d2521610", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Goal: integration by parts practice\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 5 minutes you will state a concise learning outcome for using integration by parts (one sentence) and then attempt one short worked example: ∫ x e^x dx, showing your chosen u and dv and the resulting integral.\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":5,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Write a one-sentence learning outcome (e.g., 'I will be able to apply integration by parts to integrate u·dv when u and dv are chosen appropriately').\\",\\"Choose u and dv for ∫ x e^x dx and set up the integration by parts formula.\\",\\"Carry out the integration and write the final antiderivative (plus constant).\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 36664, "completedAtMs": 36664, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends opening with a goal frame after the prerequisite check.", "Limited time and remaining moves -> pick a focused, actionable outcome (cheap commitment).", "High procedural mathematical load: an explicit practice target helps allocate time for a worked example next."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "The student states a concise learning outcome (e.g., 'I will be able to apply integration by parts to integrate u dv when u and dv are chosen appropriately') and agrees to attempt one short example (e.g., ∫ x e^x dx) as a check.", "firstContentAtMs": 36664, "studentSafeReason": "Set a short, concrete outcome so the student knows what success looks like and we can choose an appropriately-scoped worked example next.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_92bc8620", "type": "worked_example", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx", "blockId": "live_block_3_060709b3", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx\\",\\"type\\":\\"worked_example\\",\\"problemStatement\\":\\"Compute the integral ∫ x e^x dx using integration by parts. Show choice of u and dv, find du and v, apply the formula, and simplify.\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"step-1\\",\\"title\\":\\"Choose u and dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Pick u = x (a polynomial whose derivative simplifies) and dv = e^x dx (easy to integrate). This pairing follows the heuristic 'choose u to simplify when differentiated.'\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Before proceeding, predict what du will be when u = x.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv: du = 1 dx, and ∫ e^x dx = e^x so v = e^x. These give the components needed for the formula.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Predict the next algebraic expression when applying the formula u·v − ∫ v·du.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply the integration-by-parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Apply ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du. Substitute u = x, v = e^x, du = dx to get x e^x − ∫ e^x dx.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No prediction required.)\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4\\",\\"title\\":\\"Finish and simplify\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Integrate the remaining term: ∫ e^x dx = e^x. So the result is x e^x − e^x + C. Factor if desired: e^x(x − 1) + C.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No prediction required.)\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Explain in one sentence why choosing u = x and dv = e^x d