ype": "prerequisite_check", "phase": "opening", "title": "Prerequisite check: Product rule", "blockId": "live_block_1_724c7871", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Prerequisite check: Product rule\\",\\"type\\":\\"prerequisite_check\\",\\"instructions\\":\\"This quick mandatory check has 2 short questions. For each, type your answer clearly. 1) State the product rule in words or formula form. 2) Differentiate f(x)=x·sin x (show steps or the final derivative). After you submit, I'll record your responses and either proceed or offer a brief remediation if needed.\\",\\"prerequisites\\":[{\\"key\\":\\"product-rule\\",\\"label\\":\\"Product rule (must be known)\\"}],\\"detourMessage\\":\\"If your answers show gaps (for example, incorrect product rule formula or mistakes differentiating x·sin x), we'll pause and do a short remedial explanation and one guided practice differentiation before continuing to integration by parts.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 18575, "completedAtMs": 18575, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile marks the product rule as a mandatory prerequisite.", "Integration by parts directly inverts the product rule; confusion will block progress.", "Limited time — a short mandatory check is more efficient than remediating later.", "Student persona 'confidently_wrong' increases risk of unrecognized errors."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student can state the product rule and use it correctly to differentiate a simple product (e.g., d/dx[x*sin x]) and identify u and v' in a basic integration-by-parts setup.", "firstContentAtMs": 18575, "studentSafeReason": "Must confirm student knows the product rule before teaching integration by parts to avoid building on a fragile foundation.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_32171c77", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Goal: Integration by parts (6 minutes)", "blockId": "live_block_2_ec639d7e", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Goal: Integration by parts (6 minutes)\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 6 minutes you will apply and explain integration by parts to solve one integral: you should be able to restate the goal, pick u and dv for a new integral, and carry out one integration-by-parts calculation showing u, dv, du, v and the assembled result.\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":6,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Restate the goal in your own words (verbal commitment).\\",\\"Given a new integral, identify u and dv and justify your choice.\\",\\"Complete one integration-by-parts solution showing u, dv, du, v and the final evaluated integral.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 33449, "completedAtMs": 33449, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Prerequisite check passed — safe to proceed to teaching moves.", "Topic profile recommends opening with a short goal/plan before worked examples.", "Limited time and remaining moves: produce a compact, actionable goal.", "Student persona 'confidently_wrong' benefits from an explicit success criterion to reduce overconfidence."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student can (1) state the goal in their own words, (2) identify u and dv in a new integral, and (3) perform one integration by parts on a provided example correctly (showing intermediate u, dv, du, v and the assembled result).", "firstContentAtMs": 33449, "studentSafeReason": "Set a clear, timeboxed outcome so the learner knows what successful use of integration by parts will look like and to keep the next worked-example activity focused and efficient.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_ec9b7add", "type": "worked_example", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx by integration by parts", "blockId": "live_block_3_e241f7cf", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Worked example: ∫ x e^x dx by integration by parts\\",\\"type\\":\\"worked_example\\",\\"problemStatement\\":\\"Compute the indefinite integral ∫ x e^x dx using integration by parts and simplify the result.\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"step-1-choose\\",\\"title\\":\\"Choose u and dv (prediction point)\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"We must pick u and dv so that du is simpler and dv is integrable. Common guideline: let u be an algebraic factor (like x) and dv the exponential e^x dx. Before I show the chosen decomposition, quickly state which part you would choose as u.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Which part of x e^x would you pick for u? (reply with 'u = ...')\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2-differentiate-integrate\\",\\"title\\":\\"Compute du and v\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Take u = x and dv = e^x dx. Then du = dx and v = ∫ e^x dx = e^x. These are standard: derivative of x is 1, integral of e^x is e^x.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"No new prediction here — confirm: du = ? and v = ?\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3-apply-formula\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply integration-by-parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Use ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du. Substitute u = x, v = e^x, du = dx to get ∫ x e^x dx = x e^x − ∫ e^x dx.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"What does ∫ x e^x dx become after substitution?\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4-evaluate-and-simplify\\",\\"title\\":\\"Evaluate the remaining integral and simplify\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Compute the remaining integral: ∫ e^x dx = e^x. Thus ∫ x e^x dx = x e^x − e^x + C. Factor e^x if desired: e^x(x − 1) + C.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Write the simplified final answer (include + C).\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Confirm you chose u and dv intentionally, showed du and v, applied ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du correctly, and simplified to e^x(x − 1) + C.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Standard calculus textbook\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Integration by parts formula and basic integrals (∫ e^x = e^x)\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 59231, "completedAtMs": 59231, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Prerequisite and goal framing completed — safe to practice applying the procedure.", "Only one move remaining and limited time — choose a focused worked example rather than branching activities.", "Topic profile strongly recommends worked examples for procedural learning of integration by parts.", "Student persona 'confidently_wrong' benefits from guided practice with prediction points to catch overconfident errors."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student states choices for u and dv, computes du and v, assembles the integration-by-parts result, and simplifies the final expression correctly (with at most one minor arithmetic slip).", "firstContentAtMs": 59231, "studentSafeReason": "Student already passed the prerequisite and has a clear, timeboxed goal; a single, guided worked example is the most efficient next step to practice choosing u and dv and performing the steps.", "studentConsentRequired": false}], "runId": "petros-stage5-live-smoke-v1", "usage": [{"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 13161, "requestId": "be24e84f-450b-4195-9714-c3650ce032f9", "costMicros": 2650, "functionKey": "teaching.next_action.select", "inputTokens": 21640, "providerKey": "openai-live-eval", "outputTokens": 895, "validationFailures": 0}, {"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 5384, "requestId": "724c7871-fa29-4b85-8436-d8d481dcc96f", "costMicros": 1144, "functionKey": "teaching.block.render", "inputTokens": 5800, "providerKey": "openai-live-eval", "outputTokens": 279, "validationFailures": 0}, {"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 9505, "requestId": "32171c77-aa17-4b16-8ce0-367aa4806c86", "costMicros": 2146, "functionKey": "teaching.next_action.select", "inputTokens": 22066, "providerKey": "openai-live-eval", "outputTokens": 590, "validationFailures": 0}, {"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheH