e": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Learning goal: Integration by parts (7 minutes)", "blockId": "live_block_2_2c48fb14", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Learning goal: Integration by parts (7 minutes)\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 7 minutes, you'll state a clear, timeboxed learning outcome for Integration by parts: explain the integration-by-parts formula and use it to evaluate one integral; then agree to the immediate practice plan (one worked example followed by a short practice question).\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":7,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Student repeats or accepts the one-sentence learning outcome.\\",\\"Student agrees to the practice plan: worked example then one practice question.\\",\\"Ready to begin the worked example now.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 30988, "completedAtMs": 30988, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile opening pattern: after prerequisite_check the next move should be goal_frame", "Short remaining time budget — keep the goal statement brief and actionable", "Student persona repeated_struggle — explicit goal and plan reduce confusion and help focus"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student repeats or accepts a concise, timeboxed learning outcome (one sentence) and agrees to the immediate practice format (worked example followed by a short practice question).", "firstContentAtMs": 30988, "studentSafeReason": "Frame a short, timeboxed learning goal so the student knows the immediate outcome and next steps after the prerequisite check.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_ac652d08", "type": "worked_example", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Integration by parts — procedural worked example", "blockId": "live_block_3_1ee7b0bc", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Integration by parts — procedural worked example\\",\\"type\\":\\"worked_example\\",\\"problemStatement\\":\\"Evaluate the integral ∫ x e^x dx using integration by parts, showing clear stepwise work.\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"step-1\\",\\"title\\":\\"Choose u and dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Pick u = x (a polynomial) and dv = e^x dx (easy to integrate). This choice keeps du simpler than differentiating e^x and makes v straightforward to find.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Which part should we differentiate (u) and which integrate (dv)? Choose: (A) u=x, dv=e^x dx or (B) u=e^x, dv=x dx.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Compute du and v\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv: du = dx, and v = ∫ e^x dx = e^x. Record both so we can apply the formula.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No response needed) Please confirm du=dx and v=e^x.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply the integration by parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Use ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du. Substitute: ∫ x e^x dx = x·e^x − ∫ e^x · dx = x e^x − ∫ e^x dx.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"What is the integral left to evaluate after substitution? Enter the remaining integral (for example: ∫ e^x dx).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4\\",\\"title\\":\\"Evaluate remaining integral and finish\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Compute ∫ e^x dx = e^x, so the result is x e^x − e^x + C. Factor if desired: e^x(x − 1) + C. This completes the integration by parts process.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"(No response needed) Check the final simplified form e^x(x − 1) + C.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"State the final answer for ∫ x e^x dx in one line (including + C).\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Standard calculus technique\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Integration by parts formula: ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du (basic integral table)\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 48995, "completedAtMs": 48995, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile practicePattern recommends worked_example next", "Short remaining time — one worked example then a single practice item fits budget", "Student persona repeated_struggle — stepwise worked example reduces confusio