\\":\\"Correction: Plants do not take ready-made food from soil. Using light energy, they assemble glucose from carbon dioxide (from air) and water; minerals from soil help growth but are not the plant’s energy source. In short: energy and carbon come from light and CO2, not from soil 'food'.\\",\\"evidence\\":[\\"Stage 4 fixture curriculum: Photosynthesis summary — plants assemble glucose from CO2 and water using light energy.\\",\\"Common classroom demonstration: plant grown in water + light still produces growth when minerals supplied, showing energy/carbon come from light/CO2.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 13640, "completedAtMs": 13640, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile lists 'misconception_demolition' as an opening move and gives it highest weight.", "Resolved profile includes a specific misconception ('soil-food') that blocks correct conceptual understanding.", "Session is a short revise session (3 moves available) — addressing the misconception early gives high leverage.", "Learner persona 'fast_confident' benefits from a direct challenge with an explicit commitment."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner makes a brief commitment (e.g., agrees/disagrees with the statement) and provides a short justification or selection that reveals whether they hold the 'soil-food' misconception.", "firstContentAtMs": 13640, "studentSafeReason": "This move gently uncovers a common, low-risk misconception (plants get food from soil) and asks for a small commitment before correcting it—appropriate for a beginner-friendly revision session.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_7ad3d575", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Session goal: Photosynthesis (short, timeboxed)", "blockId": "live_block_2_90b9f2d5", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Session goal: Photosynthesis (short, timeboxed)\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 6 minutes, explain the core process of photosynthesis and apply that understanding to identify the main inputs and outputs for one concrete example (e.g., a leaf in sunlight).\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":6,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"I confirm this goal and I'm ready to proceed.\\",\\"After the explanation, I can name the inputs and outputs for the example.\\",\\"I can explain in one sentence why soil is not the plant's food.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 25148, "completedAtMs": 25148, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile's openingPattern recommends goal framing after addressing the misconception.", "Session is a short revise session (3 moves total); a clear timeboxed goal increases efficiency.", "Learner persona 'fast_confident' prefers explicit goals and quick application tasks.", "Prior move revealed whether the 'soil-food' misconception is present; next we align on an actionable outcome before explaining."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner agrees to the framed objective (short confirmation) and indicates readiness to proceed (e.g., 'Yes — explain and show one example I can apply').", "firstContentAtMs": 25148, "studentSafeReason": "Set a concise, shared goal so the learner knows what success looks like for this short revision session and to focus the next explanatory move.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_ef4eb5d6", "type": "diagram", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Photosynthesis concept map", "blockId": "live_block_3_3d6e45fe", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Photosynthesis concept map\\",\\"type\\":\\"diagram\\",\\"diagramType\\":\\"concept_map\\",\\"nodes\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"sunlight\\",\\"label\\":\\"Sunlight\\",\\"description\\":\\"Light energy from the Sun (photons).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"leaf_chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"Leaf → Chloroplast\\",\\"description\\":\\"Site of photosynthesis in plant leaves; contains thylakoids and stroma.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light reactions 