 appears."], "totalScore": 4.29, "transcript": {"id": "live_8bb50ea2-7327-4160-9d42-003a41ab8ec8", "goal": "revise", "seed": 42, "ended": "goal_met", "moves": [{"id": "live_move_1_4431ce83", "type": "misconception_demolition", "phase": "active", "title": "Soil-food misconception", "blockId": "live_block_1_fc8418c0", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Soil-food misconception\\",\\"type\\":\\"misconception_demolition\\",\\"misconception\\":\\"Plants take food directly from the soil (they 'eat' soil nutrients as food).\\",\\"commitmentPrompt\\":\\"Before I explain, do you agree or disagree with this statement: 'Plants get their food from the soil'? Type 'agree' or 'disagree' (or your short prediction).\\",\\"correction\\":\\"Correction: Plants do not take ready-made food from soil. They make their own food (glucose) inside their leaves by combining carbon dioxide (from air) and water (from soil) using energy from sunlight; minerals from soil help growth but are not the plant's food.\\",\\"evidence\\":[\\"Balanced summary equation: Carbon dioxide + Water + light energy → Glucose + Oxygen (shows carbon and hydrogen come from CO2 and H2O, not soil).\\",\\"Observation: Food-making structures (chloroplasts) are in leaf cells where light is captured, so the process occurs in leaves using sunlight rather than in roots taking in 'food' from soil.\\",\\"Role of soil minerals: Minerals from soil (like nitrogen, phosphorus) support growth and building tissues but are not the main chemical fuel (glucose) the plant produces.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 15031, "completedAtMs": 15031, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile lists 'soil-food' as a high-priority misconception.", "Opening pattern recommends starting with misconception demolition to prevent wasted effort later.", "Session is a revise/evaluation session so explicit correction is appropriate.", "Requires a small, low-cost commitment from the learner before revealing correction."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner agrees to attempt a short prediction/commitment and, after the activity, can state that plants make glucose from CO2 and H2O using light energy (not by taking food from soil).", "firstContentAtMs": 15031, "studentSafeReason": "This move targets a common, high-impact misconception so the learner can build an accurate model of how plants make their own food.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_621cd0eb", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Set a short-term photosynthesis goal", "blockId": "live_block_2_eb559aa4", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Set a short-term photosynthesis goal\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In one sentence, articulate a brief, timeboxed goal (within this 4-minute activity) describing what you will be able to explain or do about photosynthesis — for example: 'I will explain how plants make glucose from CO2, H2O and light.'\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":4,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Write a single clear sentence stating what you will be able to explain or do about photosynthesis.\\",\\"Ensure the sentence is timeboxed to this session (it should describe what you can achieve now or by the end of the next few minutes).\\",\\"If you can't produce a sentence, choose the suggested goal provided by the tutor and confirm you accept it.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 30082, "completedAtMs": 30082, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Opening pattern in topic profile recommends goal framing after misconception demolition.", "Session is a short revise/evaluation with limited remaining moves — keep the goal timeboxed and actionable.", "Learner just completed a commitment; follow-up should ask for a short, explicit outcome to check engagement."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner states a brief, actionable goal (one sentence) such as 'I will explain how plants make glucose from CO2, H2O and light' or selects an equivalent single-sentence outcome.", "firstContentAtMs": 30082, "studentSafeReason": "Framing a concise, timeboxed outcome focuses the learner's effort after the misconception correction and sets an achievable commitment for the session.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_3b60a275", "type": "diagram", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Concept map: Core inputs, processes and outputs of photosynthesis", "blockId": "live_block_3_170495dc", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Concept map: Core inputs, processes and outputs of photosynthesis\\",\\"type\\":\\"diagram\\",\\"diagramType\\":\\"concept_map\\",\\"nodes\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"light\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light (energy)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Visible light from the sun; provides the energy that drives the reactions in the chloroplast.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"co2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Carbon dioxide (CO2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Gas taken from the air; a carbon source for making glucose.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"label\\":\\"Water (H2O)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Taken up by roots; provides hydrogen atoms and electrons and is split during the light reactions.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"Chloroplast (site of photosynthesis)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Cell organelle where light energy is captured and used to assemble glucose from CO2 and H2O.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"Glucose (C6H12O6)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Main organic product — a carbohydrate assembled from CO2 and H2O using light energy.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"Oxygen (O2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"By-product released when water is split during the light-driven reactions.\\"}],\\"edges\\":[{\\"from\\":\\"light\\",\\"to\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"supplies energy to\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"co2\\",\\"to\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"input (carbon source)\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"to\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"input (hydrogen/electrons)\\"},{\\"from\\":\