ants get their food from the soil, or do they make it themselves using light? Reply briefly with either \\\\\\"soil\\\\\\" or \\\\\\"make it\\\\\\".\\",\\"correction\\":\\"Plants do not take finished food from the soil. In photosynthesis, they use light energy to assemble glucose from carbon dioxide (from air) and water — the soil supplies water and mineral nutrients, but not the plant's carbon-based 'food'.\\",\\"evidence\\":[\\"Plants produce glucose in their leaves by combining CO2 + H2O using light energy (this is photosynthesis).\\",\\"Soil supplies minerals and water, which support growth, but it does not provide the carbon that becomes the plant’s sugar.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 14640, "completedAtMs": 14640, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile flags a high-value misconception ('soil-food') that often causes repeated struggle.", "Session type is revision with limited moves — prioritize a focused corrective move.", "Recommended opening pattern for this topic begins with misconception_demolition."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner explicitly rejects the 'plants take food from soil' idea and explains (in their own words) that plants use light energy to assemble glucose from carbon dioxide and water, or correctly identifies one clear contradiction with the soil-food idea.", "firstContentAtMs": 14640, "studentSafeReason": "Student has a known misconception that directly blocks understanding; confronting it gently is safe and helpful.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_302ef691", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis", "blockId": "live_block_2_93854d58", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Set a short application goal for Photosynthesis\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In one sentence, state a small, task-oriented goal using the corrected model (for example: “I will explain how plants make glucose from light, CO2 and H2O”) and agree to try a single short application (e.g., label which inputs are needed in a simple scenario).\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":5,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Write a one-sentence goal that uses light, carbon dioxide and water correctly.\\",\\"Complete a single short application task (label inputs or choose the correct inputs in a brief scenario).\\",\\"Briefly confirm whether the attempted application matched your goal and note any remaining confusion.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 28300, "completedAtMs": 28300, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile's openingPattern recommends goal_frame after misconception_demolition.", "Session is time-limited with only two moves remaining — prefer a concise, high-value framing move.", "A short application check will produce clear evidence for readiness before a diagram/layered explanation."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner restates a clear, task-oriented goal (one sentence) such as 'I will explain how plants get glucose using light, CO2 and H2O' and agrees to try a single short application (e.g., label which inputs are needed for photosynthesis in a simple scenario).", "firstContentAtMs": 28300, "studentSafeReason": "After correcting the soil-food misconception, a brief goal frame focuses the learner on a small application task that reveals whether they can use the corrected idea safely and productively.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_01dca176", "type": "diagram", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Photosynthesis concept map — inputs, process, outputs", "blockId": "live_block_3_5162b625", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Photosynthesis concept map — inputs, process, outputs\\",\\"type\\":\\"diagram\\",\\"diagramType\\":\\"concept_map\\",\\"nodes\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"light\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light (energy)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Sunlight providing energy for the light reactions.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"co2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Carbon dioxide (CO2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Taken from air through leaf stomata; carbon source for glucose.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"label\\":\\"Water (H2O)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Taken up by roots; supplies electrons/H to reactions and O atoms.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"label\\":\\"Chloroplast (site)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Cell organelle where light reactions and the Calvin cycle occur.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"Light reactions\\",\\"description\\":\\"Use light to make ATP and NADPH and split water (release O2).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"Calvin cycle (carbon fixation)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Uses ATP and NADPH to assemble CO2 and H into glucose.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"Glucose (C6H12O6)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Organic product used for energy and growth.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"Oxygen (O2)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Byproduct released when water is split.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"label\\":\\"Photosynthesis (overall)\\",\\"description\\":\\"Process that converts light + CO2 + H2O into glucose and O2.\\"}],\\"edges\\":[{\\"from\\":\\"light\\",\\"to\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"drives\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"to\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"split in\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"to\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"produces\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"to\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"provides ATP/NADPH for\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"co2\\",\\"to\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"carbon source for\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"to\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"assembles into\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"to\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"contains\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"chloroplast\\",\\"to\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"contains\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"to\\":\\"light_reactions\\",\\"label\\":\\"includes\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"to\\":\\"calvin_cycle\\",\\"label\\":\\"includes\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"light\\",\\"to\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"label\\":\\"input\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"co2\\",\\"to\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"label\\":\\"input\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"h2o\\",\\"to\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"label\\":\\"input\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"to\\":\\"glucose\\",\\"label\\":\\"output\\"},{\\"from\\":\\"photosynthesis_process\\",\\"to\\":\\"oxygen\\",\\"label\\":\\"output\\"}],\\"altText\\":\\"Concept map of photosynthesis showing inputs (Light, CO2, H2O) feeding into the photosynthesis process (light reactions and Calvin cycle within chloroplasts) which produces glucose and oxygen. Edges label relationships: light drives light reactions, water is split producing O2, light reactions supply ATP/NADPH to the Calvin cycle, and CO2 is fixed into glucose.\\",\\"editable\\":true,\\"fallbackText\\":\\"Structured view: Inputs — Light (energy), CO2, H2O. Site — Chloroplast. Process — Light reactions (use light, split water, make ATP/NADPH, release O2) and Calvin cycle (use ATP/NADPH to fix CO2 into glucose). Outputs — Glucose (C6H12O6) and Oxygen (O2).\\"}", "startedAtMs": 52045, "completedAtMs": 52045, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile strongly favors a visual representation (diagram weight high) for conceptual photosynthesis.", "Only one move remains — a single, high-value visual will reveal whether the learner can place inputs/process/output correctly.", "Prior moves obtained a cheap commitment and a brief goal; now show a focused visual to consolidate.", "An editable diagram supports quick correction if the learner mislabels parts."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner either (a) correctly identifies and/or labels the inputs (light, CO2, H2O), the main process (light-driven assembly of glucose), and outputs (glucose, O2) on the map, or (b) makes a single clear mistake that can be corrected immediately.", "firstContentAtMs": 