st or confidence evidence is missing.", "detour_return:Detour lacks an explicit return to goal.", "artifact_quality:No artifact proposal appears."], "totalScore": 4.27, "transcript": {"id": "live_c3b10e85-24b6-451c-9333-1d8bc845360e", "goal": "repair", "seed": 42, "ended": "goal_met", "moves": [{"id": "live_move_1_fcc41a7e", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Confirm learning goal for French Revolution causes", "blockId": "live_block_1_c8a3e574", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Confirm learning goal for French Revolution causes\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 3 minutes, confirm whether your goal is to 'understand and apply the causes of the French Revolution' or state a different specific learning target to focus our repair session.\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":3,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Student affirms the stated goal or gives a revised, specific goal.\\",\\"Student and tutor agree the 3-minute timebox and intended outcome (understand + apply).\\",\\"Ready to move to a focused instructional move (story) within remaining time.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 11563, "completedAtMs": 11563, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends starting with a goal frame", "Session type: repair — confirm exact learning target before remediation", "Short time budget (12 minutes) — need a focused, timeboxed plan"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student confirms or clarifies the learning goal (e.g., agrees they want to understand and apply causes) or asks to change it.", "firstContentAtMs": 11563, "studentSafeReason": "Framing the goal first helps align expectations and makes later checks efficient.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_2cb6b32a", "type": "story", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Concise four‑event story of the French Revolution causes", "blockId": "live_block_2_ad84ca42", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Concise four‑event story of the French Revolution causes\\",\\"type\\":\\"story\\",\\"setup\\":\\"A short, chronological narrative linking four main causes: social inequality, economic crisis, political dysfunction, and Enlightenment ideas. Read through each event in order to see how one problem led into the next.\\",\\"events\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"e1\\",\\"label\\":\\"Social inequality and Estate structure (pre-1789)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"France was divided into three Estates: clergy, nobility, and the Third Estate (commoners). The Third Estate bore most taxes and had little political power, creating widespread resentment and a sense of injustice.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Economic crisis and fiscal strain (late 1780s)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Years of war and royal spending left the government nearly bankrupt. Poor harvests and rising bread prices hit the Third Estate hardest, turning resentment into acute hardship and increased unrest.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e3\\",\\"label\\":\\"Political dysfunction and failed reform attempts (1788–1789)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Pressure for tax reform forced Louis XVI to call the Estates‑General. Political deadlock over voting procedures and privilege blocked meaningful reform, convincing many that the old system could not solve the crisis.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e4\\",\\"label\\":\\"Spread of Enlightenment ideas and mobilization (throughout the 1780s)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Enlightenment writers promoted liberty, equality, and popular sovereignty. These ideas gave people language and goals to challenge the ancien régime, so economic pain plus political failure turned into organized action.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"Sequence: long‑standing social inequality set the moral grievance, economic collapse made suffering immediate, political failure shut down peaceful reform, and Enlightenment ideas provided the framework to turn grievance into revolution.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 25594, "completedAtMs": 25594, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic pro