ructions\\":\\"Please answer two short questions that test your ability to evaluate simple Boolean expressions and use them in conditional logic. First, quickly state whether you think you can confidently evaluate Boolean expressions (Yes / No). Then answer the two short questions below. Your answers will determine whether we continue to for-loops or pause for a brief review.\\",\\"prerequisites\\":[{\\"key\\":\\"conditions\\",\\"label\\":\\"Boolean conditions (evaluate True/False, use in if-statements)\\"}],\\"detourMessage\\":\\"If your answers show gaps, we'll pause and give a concise refresher on Boolean expressions and simple conditionals before moving on to for-loops.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 14178, "completedAtMs": 14178, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile marks 'conditions' as a strong prerequisite", "For-loops depend on understanding boolean expressions used in control flow", "Short session budget — a quick check avoids wasted teaching time"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student correctly answers 2 short questions that show they can evaluate simple Boolean expressions and use them in conditional logic.", "firstContentAtMs": 14178, "studentSafeReason": "Student must have working knowledge of Boolean conditions before learning Python for-loops to avoid confusion about loop guards and condition checks.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_04a9c5c4", "type": "predict_then_reveal", "phase": "active", "title": "Predict output of a Python for-loop", "blockId": "live_block_2_015274d0", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Predict output of a Python for-loop\\",\\"type\\":\\"predict_then_reveal\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"Consider this Python code:\\\\n\\\\nfor i in range(1, 5):\\\\n    if i % 2 == 0:\\\\n        print(i * 2)\\\\n    else:\\\\n        print(i)\\\\n\\\\nBefore you run it, predict the exact printed output (one value per line). Then give one short sentence explaining your 