 state\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Code: numbers = [3, 5, 2]\\\\nsum_so_far = 0\\\\nfor n in numbers:\\\\n    sum_so_far += n\\\\n    print(n, sum_so_far)\\\\nInitial values: numbers is [3,5,2], sum_so_far is 0. The loop will visit each element in order and update sum_so_far by adding the current n, then print the pair (n, sum_so_far).\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Before running the loop, predict what the first printed line will be (the values printed on the first iteration).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2\\",\\"title\\":\\"First iteration (prediction checkpoint)\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"On the first iteration the loop takes n = numbers[0] which is 3. sum_so_far becomes 0 + 3 = 3. The print statement outputs the current n and the updated sum_so_far.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Enter the exact text printed on the first iteration (format: n sum_so_far).\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3\\",\\"title\\":\\"Finish the remaining iterations and result\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Second iteration: n = 5, sum_so_far becomes 3 + 5 = 8, print outputs \\\\\\"5 8\\\\\\". Third iteration: n = 2, sum_so_far becomes 8 + 2 = 10, print outputs \\\\\\"2 10\\\\\\". After the loop sum_so_far is 10.\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"After confirming the first printed line, state the full sequence of printed lines for all iterations, in order.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Confirm you predicted the first printed line correctly and that the final sum_so_far is 10.\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Example code\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Small illustrative Python snippet showing sequential iteration over a list.\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 48786, "completedAtMs": 48786, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends worked_example after a prediction to consolidate mechanics", "Remaining time and one move left — a short worked example is efficient", "Prior prediction revealed readiness to practice procedural execution", "Worked example supports sequential representation of iteration"], "artifactProposed": fa