ns to show you can evaluate simple Boolean expressions and describe using a Boolean in a control statement. Keep answers brief (one line each).\\",\\"prerequisites\\":[{\\"key\\":\\"conditions\\",\\"label\\":\\"Boolean conditions\\"}],\\"detourMessage\\":\\"If you struggle with these, we will pause and quickly review Boolean expressions and comparison operators before continuing to for-loops.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 16555, "completedAtMs": 16555, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile marks 'prerequisite_check' as required for opening.", "Resolved profile lists 'Boolean conditions' as a strong prerequisite.", "Student persona indicates repeated struggle — check foundations first.", "Short remaining time budget — quick diagnostic is appropriate."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student answers two short questions showing they can (a) evaluate simple Boolean expressions and (b) use a boolean in a one-line if/for style description.", "firstContentAtMs": 16555, "studentSafeReason": "Confirming prerequisite knowledge (Boolean conditions) prevents confusion when introducing iteration and ensures examples will be at the right level.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_1ecb7f0c", "type": "predict_then_reveal", "phase": "active", "title": "Predict the output of a simple for-loop", "blockId": "live_block_2_59f9339f", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Predict the output of a simple for-loop\\",\\"type\\":\\"predict_then_reveal\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"Look at this Python code. Before I show the result, write a one-line prediction of exactly what will be printed (including order and punctuation). Commit to a short answer first.\\\\n\\\\nfor i in range(3):\\\\n    print(i)\\\\n\\\\nYour one-line prediction:\\",\\"reveal\\":\\"The program prints three lines with the numbers 0, 1, and 2 in order. Exact printed output:\\\\n0\\\\n1\\\\n2\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"range(3) produces the sequence 0, 1, 2. 