ntiated and dv as the remaining part that you can integrate easily. For integrals like x e^x, choose u = x (because du is simple) and dv = e^x dx (because v is e^x).\\",\\"predictionPrompt\\":\\"Before proceeding, state which choice you would make for u and dv for ∫ x e^x dx.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Differentiate u and integrate dv\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Differentiate u: u = x ⇒ du = dx. Integrate dv: dv = e^x dx ⇒ v = e^x. These give the pieces needed for the formula ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-3\\",\\"title\\":\\"Apply integration by parts formula\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Substitute into the formula: ∫ x e^x dx = u v − ∫ v du = x e^x − ∫ e^x dx. The remaining integral ∫ e^x dx is straightforward to evaluate.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"step-4\\",\\"title\\":\\"Evaluate and simplify\\",\\"explanation\\":\\"Compute the remaining integral: ∫ e^x dx = e^x. Thus ∫ x e^x dx = x e^x − e^x + C. Factor if desired: = e^x(x − 1) + C.\\"}],\\"finalCheck\\":\\"Write the final simplified antiderivative for ∫ x e^x dx (include the constant of integration).\\",\\"sourceGrounding\\":[{\\"label\\":\\"Integration by parts formula\\",\\"reference\\":\\"Standard calculus identity: ∫ u dv = u v − ∫ v du\\"}]}", "startedAtMs": 77834, "completedAtMs": 77834, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends a worked_example next in the practice pattern", "Prerequisite check failed, so procedural scaffolding and immediate practice are needed", "Only one move remaining in this timebox—prefer a single compact worked example with a small prediction step", "Keep the example procedural and exam-shaped to match syllabus expectations"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student chooses u and dv correctly for the worked example, computes ∫u dv → uv − ∫v du, and produces the simplified final value (or a correct intermediate decomposition) in a short-answer form.", "firstContentAtMs": 77834, "studentSafeReason": "Student showed incorrect / low‑