move_2_2cb6b32a", "type": "story", "phase": "explaining", "title": "Concise four‑event story of the French Revolution causes", "blockId": "live_block_2_ad84ca42", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Concise four‑event story of the French Revolution causes\\",\\"type\\":\\"story\\",\\"setup\\":\\"A short, chronological narrative linking four main causes: social inequality, economic crisis, political dysfunction, and Enlightenment ideas. Read through each event in order to see how one problem led into the next.\\",\\"events\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"e1\\",\\"label\\":\\"Social inequality and Estate structure (pre-1789)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"France was divided into three Estates: clergy, nobility, and the Third Estate (commoners). The Third Estate bore most taxes and had little political power, creating widespread resentment and a sense of injustice.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Economic crisis and fiscal strain (late 1780s)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Years of war and royal spending left the government nearly bankrupt. Poor harvests and rising bread prices hit the Third Estate hardest, turning resentment into acute hardship and increased unrest.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e3\\",\\"label\\":\\"Political dysfunction and failed reform attempts (1788–1789)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Pressure for tax reform forced Louis XVI to call the Estates‑General. Political deadlock over voting procedures and privilege blocked meaningful reform, convincing many that the old system could not solve the crisis.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e4\\",\\"label\\":\\"Spread of Enlightenment ideas and mobilization (throughout the 1780s)\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Enlightenment writers promoted liberty, equality, and popular sovereignty. These ideas gave people language and goals to challenge the ancien régime, so economic pain plus political failure turned into organized action.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"Sequence: long‑standing social inequality set the moral grievance, economic collapse made suffering immediate, political failure shut down peaceful reform, and Enlightenment ideas provided the framework to turn grievance into revolution.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 25594, "completedAtMs": 25594, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends starting with a story after goal framing", "Session type: repair — provide a clear, corrected narrative to replace gaps", "Short time remaining — use a concise, focused story (4 events) to cover main causes", "Follow-up checks (contrast_case, recall_check) are available in remaining moves"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student can list or paraphrase the main causes (e.g., social inequality, economic crisis, political dysfunction, Enlightenment ideas) and place them in a short sequence or explain one cause's role.", "firstContentAtMs": 25594, "studentSafeReason": "A brief narrative (story) will reconnect key factual causes in an organised, memorable sequence appropriate for repair work.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_7b79fe0d", "type": "recall_check", "phase": "active", "title": "Recall check: French Revolution causes", "blockId": "live_block_3_97ca0d60", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Recall check: French Revolution causes\\",\\"type\\":\\"recall_check\\",\\"instructions\\":\\"Please answer both prompts briefly. Aim for a short list for Q1 and one or two sentences for Q2.\\",\\"questions\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"q1\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"List the main causes of the French Revolution (brief bullet or comma-separated list).\\",\\"responseType\\":\\"short_answer\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"q2\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"In one or two sentences, explain how one of those causes helped trigger the revolution.\\",\\"responseType\\":\\"short_answer\\"}],\\"answerContract\\":{\\"completion\\":\\"all_questions_answered\\",\\"responseHandling\\":\\"record_only_stage_2\\"},\\"feedback\\":{\\"submittedMessage\\":\\"Thanks — your answers are recorded. I will use them to decide any next steps.\\",\\"stageBoundary\\":\\"After you submit, I will check your responses and recommend the next move.\\"}}", "startedAtMs": 42798, "completedAtMs": 42798, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Session is repair-focused — need an inexpensive elicitation to check corrected knowledge", "Topic profile recommends recall_check as a follow-up to story", "Short remaining time and only one move left — keep it brief (2 short-answer questions)", "No specific misconception was observed yet, so start with retrieval before remediation"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Student answers two short prompts: (1) lists the main causes (e.g., social inequality, economic crisis, political dysfunction, Enlightenment ideas), and (2) briefly explains how one cause contributed to the outbreak (one or two sentences).", "firstContentAtMs": 42798, "studentSafeReason": "A quick recall check asks for a small, concrete commitment and reveals whether repair succeeded without imposing heavy work.", "studentConsentRequired": false}], "runId": "petros-stage5-live-smoke-v1", "usage": [{"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 7719, "requestId": "fcc41a7e-631b-4c4a-b433-bbca7da6cf78", "costMicros": 2380, "functionKey": "teaching.next_action.select", "inputTokens": 21753, "providerKey": "openai-live-eval", "outputTokens": 746, "validationFailures": 0}, {"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 3823, "requestId": "c8a3e574-3561-41f0-9e82-4bf09bdff746", "costMicros": 1118, "functionKey": "teaching.block.render", "inputTokens": 5775, "providerKey": "openai-live-eval", "outputTokens": 269, "validationFailures": 0}, {"source": "evaluation", "retries": 0, "cacheHit": false, "modelKey": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "fallbacks": 0, "latencyMs": 8592, "requestId": "2cb6b32a-5042-471a-901a-211bea6786a2", "costMicros": 2697, "funct