402cdaa5-fbab-40ea-a7e2-ff5f688cb6e4	392e146e-92d3-486c-a4f3-efa54a628127	live_9937d9f7-bdb1-43b2-bbb0-ff60573a5d10	pq-03-french-revolution	topic:french-revolution	French Revolution causes	History	repeated_struggle	repair	42	428	failed	["stuck_recovery:The struggle ladder is incomplete or does not end in success."]	["guess_confidence:Guess-first or confidence evidence is missing.", "artifact_quality:No artifact proposal appears."]	{"id": "live_9937d9f7-bdb1-43b2-bbb0-ff60573a5d10", "goal": "repair", "seed": 42, "ended": "goal_met", "moves": [{"id": "live_move_1_a61485f2", "type": "goal_frame", "phase": "opening", "title": "Set a focused goal for studying causes of the French Revolution", "blockId": "live_block_1_edd25098", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Set a focused goal for studying causes of the French Revolution\\",\\"type\\":\\"goal_frame\\",\\"goal\\":\\"In the next 6 minutes, articulate and apply at least one key cause of the French Revolution to a very short example (one sentence of your own).\\",\\"timeEstimateMinutes\\":6,\\"checkpoints\\":[\\"Write one one-sentence learning goal about what you want to learn right now.\\",\\"Choose one specific cause of the French Revolution you want to focus on (e.g., economic inequality, political corruption, Enlightenment ideas, or social structure).\\",\\"Apply that chosen cause to a short example: write one sentence showing how that cause could lead to popular unrest or a specific event.\\"]}", "startedAtMs": 11056, "completedAtMs": 11056, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["opening move to set clear outcome", "topic profile recommends goal_frame as opener", "student labelled 'repeated_struggle' so clear targets help engagement"], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner states a focused learning goal in their own words (one sentence) and selects one cause they'd like to focus on applying to a short example.", "firstContentAtMs": 11056, "studentSafeReason": "Safe to proceed: introductory framing to focus on key causes and align expectations.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_2_898eb7b8", "type": "story", "phase": "explaining", "title": "A Parisian family's view: causes of the French Revolution", "blockId": "live_block_2_3cd1b7ab", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"A Parisian family's view: causes of the French Revolution\\",\\"type\\":\\"story\\",\\"setup\\":\\"A short first-person vignette from the perspective of Jeanne, a member of a working-class Parisian family in the 1780s, showing daily life strained by rising prices, heavy taxes, and lack of political voice.\\",\\"events\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"e1\\",\\"label\\":\\"Empty bread basket\\",\\"detail\\":\\"I wake to find our bread ration smaller than last week. Flour prices have jumped and my husband's wages can't keep up, so we skip meals and worry each day about feeding the children.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e2\\",\\"label\\":\\"Crushing taxes\\",\\"detail\\":\\"A tax collector passes through and demands more than before. The nobles and clergy seem exempt, while we pay again and again. I resent that money leaves our pocket but brings no relief.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e3\\",\\"label\\":\\"No voice at the town meeting\\",\\"detail\\":\\"At the local meeting I try to raise our problems, but only the wealthy landowners are invited to decide taxes and laws. My words are ignored—we have no seat where decisions are made.\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"e4\\",\\"label\\":\\"Rumors and anger spread\\",\\"detail\\":\\"Neighbors talk of hunger, of debts, and of how others live tax-free. People gather in the square, angry and ready to demand change; I feel fear, but also a fierce hope that things must be fixed.\\"}],\\"takeaway\\":\\"Jeanne's story highlights three key causes often linked to the French Revolution: severe economic hardship for ordinary people, an unfair and heavy tax burden largely borne by the commoners, and political exclusion from decision-making. These combined pressures helped push many people toward demanding major change.\\"}", "startedAtMs": 27508, "completedAtMs": 27508, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends 'story' as the second opening move after goal framing.", "Learner persona 'repeated_struggle' benefits from narrative anchoring and reduced abstraction.", "Low prerequisite density and low misconception richness — a focused illustrative story will aid recall.", "Timebox and remaining moves favour a single short, scaffolded example rather than multiple problems."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner identifies at least one key cause mentioned in the story and applies it (one or two sentences) to a short example or micro-scenario provided.", "firstContentAtMs": 27508, "studentSafeReason": "Story move is appropriate: engages learner by placing causes in a narrative context and provides a concrete example to apply a cause.", "studentConsentRequired": false}, {"id": "live_move_3_85ac6eb1", "type": "contrast_case", "phase": "active", "title": "Contrast: economic vs political causes", "blockId": "live_block_3_789363b6", "content": "{\\"schemaVersion\\":\\"petros.render.v2\\",\\"title\\":\\"Contrast: economic vs political causes\\",\\"type\\":\\"contrast_case\\",\\"left\\":{\\"label\\":\\"Scenario A — Fiscal hardship & taxation\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"A Parisian shopkeeper struggles as bread prices soar and new royal taxes eat into family income. The crown borrows heavily, and collectors forcibly take goods when taxes fall unpaid. Does this scenario best illustrate a fiscal/economic cause of unrest? Explain briefly which feature makes it an economic cause.\\",\\"method\\":\\"Pick YES if this scenario matches the fiscal hardship/taxation cause; then justify in 1–2 sentences by naming the key economic feature (e.g., heavy taxation, state debt, rising bread prices).\\"},\\"right\\":{\\"label\\":\\"Scenario B — Political exclusion & lack of representation\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"A skilled craftsman watches local notables and nobles pass laws at salons and in courts while the Third Estate has no real voice. Requests for fairer representation are ignored and assembly seats are limited by birth. Does this scenario best illustrate political exclusion as a cause? Explain briefly which feature makes it a political cause.\\",\\"method\\":\\"Pick YES if this scenario matches political exclusion/representation as the cause; then justify in 1–2 sentences by naming the key political feature (e.g., lack of representation, privileged estates, denied political voice).\\"},\\"keyDistinction\\":\\"Decide which scenario matches the named cause by identifying the central distinguishing feature: economic hardship (taxes, debt, bread prices) versus political exclusion (no representation, privileged estates).\\"}", "startedAtMs": 45599, "completedAtMs": 45599, "sourceAnchors": [], "decisionFactors": ["Topic profile recommends contrast_case after the story in the practicePattern.", "Learner persona 'repeated_struggle' benefits from focused comparisons that surface distinguishing features.", "Only one move remaining — a single targeted contrast case provides high value practice and diagnostic information.", "Low misconception richness means a contrast will be concise and unlikely to introduce confusion."], "artifactProposed": false, "expectedEvidence": "Learner explains (1–2 sentences) which of two short micro-scenarios from the contrast exemplifies a key cause (e.g., fiscal crisis vs. political exclusion) and justifies their choice by naming the distinguishing feature.", "firstContentAtMs": 45599, "studentSafeReason": "Contrast case is safe and appropriate: it helps the learner distinguish similar causes and apply reasoning after the story, fits the topic profile's recommended practice pattern, and uses low prerequisite density so no new background is required.", "studentConsentRequired": false}], "runId": "petros-stage5-live-smoke-v1", "usag